As for the 30-second preview of the song, you can use the `preview` field in the `Song` data class, which is a URL for the preview. You can use a library like ExoPlayer to play the preview when the user clicks on the item. Here's an example of how you can do this:

1. Add the ExoPlayer dependency in your app `build.gradle`:

```groovy
dependencies {
    ...
    implementation 'com.google.android.exoplayer:exoplayer:2.16.1'
}
```

2. Create a function to play the preview when an `AlbumDetailItem` is clicked:

```kotlin
private fun playPreview(context: Context, previewUrl: String) {
    val player = SimpleExoPlayer.Builder(context).build()
    val mediaItem = MediaItem.fromUri(previewUrl)
    player.setMediaItem(mediaItem)
    player.prepare()
    player.playWhenReady = true

    // Stop playing after 30 seconds
    player.seekTo(30000)
    player.addListener(object : Player.Listener {
        override fun onPositionDiscontinuity(
            oldPosition: PlaybackStateCompat.PositionInfo,
            newPosition: PlaybackStateCompat.PositionInfo,
            reason: Int
        ) {
            if (newPosition.windowIndex != oldPosition.windowIndex) {
                player.stop()
                player.release()
            }
        }
    })
}
```

3. Update the `AlbumDetailItem` composable to call `playPreview` when the item is clicked:

```kotlin
val context = LocalContext.current
.clickable(onClick = {
    navController.navigate("songDetail/${song.id}")
    playPreview(context, song.preview)
})
```

This will play the preview when you click on the album detail item, and navigate to the song detail screen.

